     </DOKIL>
     <HEAD>
      <TDOBJECT>DOKU</TDOBJECT>
      <TDNAME>/CTDI/PRINT_REPAIR</TDNAME>
      <TDID>RE</TDID>
      <TDSPRAS>E</TDSPRAS>
      <TDFUSER>DEVELOPER</TDFUSER>
      <TDFRELES>750</TDFRELES>
      <FUSER>DEVELOPER</FUSER>
      <FRELES>750</FRELES>
     </HEAD>
     <LINES>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;PURPOSE&amp;</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>The /CTDI/PRINT_REPAIR program is the dynamic routing and execution</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> orchestrator for Repair Printouts. It is built upon the logic of</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> the legacy /CELLAG/ALCAREP02 report, extending it with flexible</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> routing capabilities. Once the testing phase is successfully</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> completed, this framework is intended to replace /CELLAG/ALCAREP02</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> entirely.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>FEATURES</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Dynamic output determination based on customizing table /CTDI/REP_FORMS.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Fallback access sequences matching VB/Contract, SKZ, and AKZ to</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> determine print drivers.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Backward compatibility with legacy routines (ALCAREP02 / print_old)</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> via exception handling.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Structured logging using the standard application log wrapper</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> /CTDI/CL_PRINT_DRIVER_LOG.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>HOW TO EXTEND DATA LOGIC</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>To extend the data retrieval or formatting logic for a specific</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> customer or project:</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>1. Create a subclass inheriting from base class</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> /CTDI/CL_PRINT_DRIVER_BASE.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>2. Redefine and implement the protected action hook methods:</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>* </TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> - unpack_io_data: Extract input/output parameters from execution</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>   context.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>* </TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> - fetch_data_from_db: Select necessary data from database tables.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>* </TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> - map_and_register_data: Map internal data and register custom</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>   parameters.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>3. Register custom form parameters in the hook map_and_register_data</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>   using method register_custom_parameter.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Ensure to pass the explicit parameter kind (e.g.,</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> abap_func_exporting, abap_func_tables) to avoid runtime DB lookups.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>HOW TO EXTEND PROCESS LOGIC</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>To change or add routing logic:</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>1. Maintain configuration entries in customizing table /CTDI/REP_FORMS</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>   via transaction SM30.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>2. Define the form layout name (Smart Form or Adobe Form) and map it</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>   to your new print driver class.</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>3. Use the class skeleton generator in customizing engine class</TDLINE>
      </item>
      <item>
       <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE> /CTDI/CL_PRINT_CUST_ENGINE to auto-generate class stubs in DEV.</TDLINE>
      </item>
     </LINES>
    </item>
